  "text": "(1) Limitations on hours and days of operation (which limitations may, in an\nappropriate case, permit haul hours outside 7:00 a.m. to 7:00 p.m.).\n(2) Limitations on truck weight, length and width.\n(3) Limitations on numbers of haul trips ALLOWED UNDER A SINGLE PERMIT.\n(4) Limitation on duration of permit.\n(4) Location and parking of construction worker vehicles.\n(5) Requirements for flag persons.\n(6) Limitations on route, schedule, and duration of activities.\n(7) Any other condition required for public safety.\n(8) Mitigation requirements, including but not limited to grading, resurfacing, bridge\nimprovements or repair, and the posting of security for the same.\n(9)\nPayment in advance for review of the application by professionals, including the\nTown Attorney, and Engineer ENGINEERS, AND OTHERS AS NEEDED FOR\nCOMPLEX OR HIGH IMPACT APPLICATIONS.\n(10)\nPERFORMANCE BOND, LETTER OF CREDIT OR OTHER ACCEPTABLE\nFINANCIAL SECURITY, IN AN AMOUNT ESTABLISHED BY THE\nADMINISTRATOR FOR HIGH-VOLUME HAULING OPERATIONS.\n(11) REQUIRED PRE-AND POST-HAUL PHOTOGRAPHIC DOCUMENTATION\nOF APPROVED HAUL ROUTES FOR PROJECTS EXCEEDING 6 TRIPS.\n(12) REQUIRED SUBMISSION OF A TRAFFIC MANAGEMENT PLAN,\nINCLUDING FLAGGING OPERATIONS, WHEN DEEMED NECESSARY BY\nTHE TOWN ADMINISTRATOR.\n(13) REQUIRED SCHOOL TRANSPORTATION CONFLICT MANAGEMENT\nPLAN WHEN HAULING ACTIVITIES MAY AFFECT SCHOOL BUS\nROUTES, STUDENT TRAVEL TIMES, OR STUDENT PICKUP OR DROP-\nOFF TIMES.\n(14)\nREQUIREMENTS ESTABLISHED BY THE TOWN ADMINISTRATOR\nREGARDING THE PARKING AND STAGING OF CONSTRUCTION\nWORKER VEHICLES.\nSection 7.\nEffective Date. This ordinance shall take effect upon final adoption as\nprovided by Section 5.26 of the Territorial Charter.\nINTRODUCED, READ, APPROVED AND ORDERED POSTED IN FULL ON\nFIRST READING on the 23day of June\n2026.\nINTRODUCED ON SECOND READING, FINALLY ADOPTED AND ORDERED\nPOSTED AFTER PUBLIC HEARING on the 13 day of August\n_2026.\n3",
